{"id": "EUVD-2026-95109", "enisaUuid": "b755c5f7-2922-3fb7-8abf-2f495a1f3c7b", "description": "msgpack5 is a msgpack v5 implementation for node.js and the browser. Prior to 6.1.0, the array and map decoding paths have no nesting-depth limit, allowing an attacker who can provide MessagePack input to submit deeply nested containers that exhaust the JavaScript call stack and interrupt a process, worker, or request handler. This issue is fixed in version 6.1.0.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T17:08:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T11:39:42", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://github.com/mcollina/msgpack5/security/advisories/GHSA-24ch-f2g6-9hhh", "https://github.com/mcollina/msgpack5/commit/1e2b5874e555dd7c99417f64788a03b0590bb102", "https://github.com/mcollina/msgpack5/releases/tag/v6.1.0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107298", "GHSA-24ch-f2g6-9hhh"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cc6a1ae3-8a40-3411-83a0-a38c08ad09f1", "product": {"name": "msgpack5", "vendor": {"name": "mcollina"}}, "product_version": "< 6.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ad162014-a803-3d74-a1a7-66f2e7ba7f2d", "vendor": {"name": "mcollina"}}], "isExploited": false}